# Accessibility

- **Images**: Every `<img>` must have a meaningful `alt` (e.g. `${experience.company} logo`). Decorative images can use `alt=""` and `role="presentation"` if appropriate.
- **Semantic HTML**: Use heading levels in order (h1 → h2 → h3). Use `<nav>`, `<main>`, `<section>`, `<article>` where they improve structure.
- **Optional content**: If a field is optional (e.g. `location?`), do not render the label/icon when the value is missing. Omit the whole block (icon + text) instead of showing an empty or "undefined" value.
- **Focus**: Preserve visible focus states on interactive elements; avoid removing outlines unless replacing with a clear focus style.
